invariant: INV-39
file: tcp_nonblocking_step.c
catches: tcp_nonblocking_loop_test
reason: the tcp-nonblocking client completes on a server Finished that has
  bytes after it in its record, and drops them when it resets cfg.buf for
  ch_read. RFC 9846 section 5.1 makes that unexpected_message.
  test/tcp_nonblocking_record_end_tests.h seals the Finished again with one
  byte after it and requires that alert.

--- old
    // And after the server Finished, before the epoch commit and the
    // client Finished, as handshake.c orders it.
    rc = hsr_check_record_end(&r->hs);
    if (rc != CH_OK) {
        return rc;
    }
--- new
